<title>CANADA: PanCanadian Q4 share profit soars.</title>
<headline>PanCanadian Q4 share profit soars.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			  1995</p>
<p> Shr			 C$0.97		   C$0.28</p>
<p> Net			122,200		   35,200</p>
<p> Cash flow/shr	     2.68		     1.68</p>
<p> Revs		     951,600		  583,900</p>
<p>	   YEAR</p>
<p> Shr			 C$2.75		   C$1.82</p>
<p> Net			345,800		  227,800</p>
<p> Cash flow/shr	     7.97		     6.42</p>
<p> Revs		   2,786,000		1,850,900</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 125,500		  125,300</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: PanCanadian Petroleum Ltd said that as a result of tax-planning initiatives, improved results from Canadian operations and a review of current provisions, it recognized a net gain of C$20.5 million in the fourth quarter of 1996 and C$65.1 million for the full year.</p>
<p>Information provided for 1995 has been reclassified to conform to the presentation adopted in 1996.</p>
<p>PanCanadian is 87-percent owned by Canadian Pacific Ltd.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
